WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.453
Gate five is Google Cloud's
Personalized Service Health,

2
00:00:03.453 --> 00:00:07.362
which lists the incidents relevant
to a project or organization.

3
00:00:07.362 --> 00:00:10.549
Google's documentation
sets one hard limit:

4
00:00:10.549 --> 00:00:13.825
the API has a single
event category, incident.

5
00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:17.964
Planned maintenance isn't in it, so
this gate covers incidents only,

6
00:00:17.964 --> 00:00:21.050
and the gap is recorded
with the security officer.

7
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.910
The project owner enables the API once and

8
00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.688
grants the reader's group the viewer role.

9
00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:30.201
Then cross-check with Google's
own list command, and collect.

10
00:00:30.201 --> 00:00:31.567
For an organization,

11
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:35.750
the settings say so and the role
is granted on the organization.

12
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.244
But the gcloud flags for
organization events weren't read,

13
00:00:39.244 --> 00:00:43.175
so the kit marks that call unverified
and runs it only when told to.

14
00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:47.491
And for government workloads: Google's
Assured Workloads page lists this

15
00:00:47.491 --> 00:00:51.737
product under regional packages, but
not under FedRAMP Moderate or High.

16
00:00:51.737 --> 00:00:54.980
A workload in those packages
has nothing to read here.
